*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
# Exception: the project-local debug keystore is committed so every checkout /
# CI build / local build signs `./gradlew installDebug` with the same key —
# otherwise each machine's generated ~/.android/debug.keystore would force a
# full uninstall on the device before each update.
!app/monotrypt-debug.keystore

# External native build folder generated in Android Studio 2.2 and later
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# NDK
obj/

# Mac
.DS_Store

# VS Code
# The contents, not the directory: a rule that excludes a directory outright
# cannot be re-opened for one file inside it, and extensions.json is committed
# on purpose so a checkout gets the recommended extensions.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Custom AI Assistant files — agent team is version-controlled.
# Keep machine-local settings and runtime agent memory out of git.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agent-memory/

# Custom project files
compile_errors.txt
monochrome-autoeq-alpha.apk
monochrome_tf_reference-*.pdf
# Scratch files land at the repo root — a pasted compile log, an exported CSV,
# a downloaded font. These are anchored with a leading slash so they mean "at
# the root" and nothing more.
#
# They used to be unanchored, which made them match every .txt/.csv/.ttf/.json
# /.py in the tree and required a negation per committed asset. Nineteen of
# those accumulated, and the twentieth was forgotten: the Glyph pack shipped
# without its manifest, so a fresh clone drew fallback squares for all 117
# assets and only CI noticed. Anchoring is what stops the next one.
/*.txt
/*.csv
/*.ttf
/*.json
/*.py
old_HomeViewModel.kt
!monochrome-library-2026-03-23.json
# The genre graph's source and build/validate scripts. The committed JSON assets
# above are generated from these, so without them the dataset is unmaintainable.
# The stem model catalogue the app fetches, and the script that writes it. The
# script is what keeps the url, size and hash off anyone's keyboard, so losing
# it would mean hand-editing a checksum — a wrong one is indistinguishable from
# a corrupt download once published.
# The two research caches the build reads and never regenerates on its own:
# Last.fm tag reach, and the Wikipedia histories. Both are the *input* to a
# build, not its output — the blanket *.json rule was quietly excluding the
# reach cache, so rebuilding the graph on a fresh clone dropped the popularity
# figures from all 771 genres and there was no way to get them back without a
# four-minute refetch. Committed, a build is reproducible offline and produces
# the same asset every time, which is the whole reason the caches exist.
# The world radio globe: the same three-stage shape, plus its two inputs. The
# GeoNames gazetteer zip is deliberately *not* here — it is 3 MB, it is a
# download rather than a decision, and fetch_world_radio.py re-fetches it on
# demand.
# The gazetteer download itself stays out: 3 MB, re-fetched on demand.
tools/cities15000.zip
# The bundled font library. Caught by the blanket *.ttf and *.txt rules above,
# but these ship in the APK — and the licence file has to travel with the fonts
# it covers, so it is not optional.

# Local Claude Code guidance (untracked by request)
CLAUDE.md
tools/__pycache__/

# Design canvas sources. The seeded .html is 2 MB of build output and stays
# ignored; the .dc.html artboards, the generator and the layout are the inputs
# that rebuild it, and they are caught by the blanket *.html / *.py / *.json
# rules above without these.
.design/**/*.html
!.design/**/*.dc.html
